## Seams

### Picked up from Grade 4 computer science

Every grade 5 row assumes a grade 4 row, taught the year before in grade 4 computer science
(docs/courses/computer-science-grade-4/frame.md), so each opens as a retrieval task inside the first session that
needs it (lesson 16), never as a readiness check or a reteach. The grade 4 unit and its course days (one a week, so
day n is week n) are given for each row (lesson 18).

| Grade 4 row (last use: grade 4 computer science, unit and days) | What it gave | Picked up here | Treatment |
|---|---|---|---|
| g4-troubleshoot (unit 1, days 1 to 6) | A troubleshooting process on staged faults, placed on the system-diagram | Unit 1 session 1 (g5-hardware-software) | Retrieval: name the part a staged fault sits in on the system-diagram |
| g4-wired-wireless (unit 1, days 1 to 6) | Two network-diagrams of one room compared | Unit 1 session 2 (g5-network-parts) | Retrieval: say one way a cable and one way wireless is better |
| g4-authn-authz (unit 1, days 1 to 6) | Proving who you are versus what you may open | Unit 1 session 3 (g5-cia-triad) | Retrieval: sort two cards, proving who versus allowed to open |
| g4-written-algorithm (unit 2, days 7 to 10) | A written algorithm with sequence, event, repeat and choice in numbered sentences (step-card) | Unit 2 session 1 (g5-visual-algorithm) | Retrieval: trace a four-line written algorithm, then the same steps become boxes |
| g4-algorithm-groups (unit 2, days 7 to 10) | Two algorithms for one job weighed for who each helps (benefit-risk-chart) | Unit 2 session 3 (g5-human-centered) | Retrieval: who did one grade 4 rule help or leave out |
| g4-trace-values (unit 4, days 19 to 23) | Trace-table of a counting loop and a score; named-box | Unit 3 session 1 (g5-variables-use) | Retrieval: three-minute trace of a counter |
