{"strand": "data", "grade": "5", "skill_id": "g5-variability", "standard": "E5-DAT-DI-10", "assumes": "g4-data-explain", "hands_on": "g6-data-quality", "model_in": "data-table; data-visualization", "model_out": "data-table; data-visualization", "words": "variability; spread; outlier; cause; measure; typical; different", "cross_subject": "science:s5-design-test", "notes": "Device and unplugged day. A given dataset (plant growth, sound levels, daily temperatures) is analyzed for how much values differ and where the differences may come from (measuring error, different conditions, real change). Students mark the outlier and say a possible source. Students mark typical values and the outlier and name one relationship between two columns; no mean or other statistic is computed."}
{"strand": "data", "grade": "5", "skill_id": "g5-data-benefits-risks", "standard": "E5-DAT-IM-11", "assumes": "g4-data-people", "hands_on": "g6-data-about-people", "model_in": "data-table; benefit-risk-chart", "model_out": "data-table; benefit-risk-chart", "words": "collected data; benefit; risk; purpose; trust; protect; limit", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Unplugged day. Case cards of a technology that uses collected data (a route planner, a recommendation list, a fitness count). Students fill a benefit-risk-chart and say who gains, who is at risk and one limit that would make it safer."}
{"strand": "programming", "grade": "5", "skill_id": "g5-remix-program", "standard": "E5-PRO-PD-04", "assumes": "g4-compare-solutions", "hands_on": "g6-procedures", "model_in": "block-program; block-and-text-view", "model_out": "block-program; block-and-text-view", "words": "remix; combine; modify; existing; credit; new; idea", "cross_subject": "", "notes": "Device day. Students start with a working program, modify it and combine it with a part of another to make a novel one, crediting the source in a comment. A worked remix is traced first. Ten lines at most. Paper stand-in: cut and paste a printed program into a new one."}
